{"title":"Arithmetic","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Arithmetic</b> is a branch of mathematics which deals with numbers and their basic properties under the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Operation\" title=\"Operation\">operations</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Addition\" title=\"Addition\">addition</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Subtraction\" title=\"Subtraction\">subtraction</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multiplication\" title=\"Multiplication\">multiplication</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Division\" title=\"Division\">division</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Exponentiation\" title=\"Exponentiation\">exponentiation</a> as well as <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Percent\" title=\"Percent\">percents</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radical\" title=\"Radical\">radicals</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fraction\" title=\"Fraction\">fractions</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Decimal\" title=\"Decimal\">decimals</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Basic_Arithmetic\">Basic Arithmetic</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Basic Arithmetic\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Some of the basic functions of arithmetic, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Addition\" title=\"Addition\">addition</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Subtraction\" title=\"Subtraction\">subtraction</a>, as well as <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multiplication\" title=\"Multiplication\">multiplication</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Division\" title=\"Division\">division</a>, relate to each other. For instance, the following are identities in arithmetic:\n</p><p>For all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, \n</p><p>...if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/2844bbe4e08e7e609f81ad97cb2cf75faae34b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e341c9179411742a33c10fc05259417eea73e9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c-b=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/240050f9af8903683875930e6edfafdfed3f0585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c-a=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />:\n...if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c966be491ad1ebdc6a022d8a7bc2ed7ce8d41340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=c$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93dfc3b49dbdb5cf5689e5e9888f50670bb3b4ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=a/b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/0/df04065965e09f95b737734ed8ccfb4a5b603cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=b/a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/9224b1b97c2a96dffd972fb14d9cc3d09374bfbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p>as well as the distributive property, which states that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5ead56154d9869528c81c8b4e651c406b19d053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(b+c)=ab+ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>There is an order to arithmetic as well, called PEMDAS, which is also commonly known as the order of operations. It shows the order in which to perform arithmetic expressions. The PEMDAS order is as follows;\n</p><p>1. Do everything inside of parentheses first.\n2. Do exponents; with \"inner\" exponents first. For example, the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb6d8d5dce21eca9893f95252d514e3c160dfe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{7^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" /> is interpreted as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8ea22568dfd1418954b5f5a9dfd5fc604de4507b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{49}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> instead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9ec28c417df014237893bdbe35294d509a5758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" />.\n3. Do multiplication and division, from left to right. For instance, the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/b/11b41897bfc90f46b6e25dbbde9a64717bbec015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\times 7 \\div 2 \\times 7 = 42 \\div 2 \\times 7= 21 \\times 7 = 147$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"335\" height=\"15\" />.\n4. Do addition and subtraction, from left to right. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42cd6dd2df44e125f9794278aaf43e19f265c995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$143-9+43 = 134+43=177$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"244\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Arithmetic_and_Number_Theory\">Arithmetic and Number Theory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Arithmetic and Number Theory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In general, more basic properties of the integers belong to arithmetic while deeper or more difficult results belong to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\">number theory</a>, but the boundary is not extremely clear. For instance, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modular_arithmetic\" title=\"Modular arithmetic\">modular arithmetic</a> might be considered part of arithmetic as well as part of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\">number theory</a>.  \n</p><p>One of the earlier arithmetic devices was the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Abacus\" title=\"Abacus\">abacus</a>.\n</p><p>Arithmetic comes from the Greek word arithmos, \"number\" and tiké [téchne], \"art\")\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Number Theory</li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018073444\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 113/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 271/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2862/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.329      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.329      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in 